{
  "id": "central-conflict",
  "term": "central conflict",
  "definition": "Central conflict refers to a brain-based signalling process involved in response inhibition, especially when a person must stop or override an action. In this source, reduced central conflict signalling is linked with poorer behavioural inhibition in some externalizing disorders.",
